            <note corresp="#d198-f8" n="4" xml:id="d198-f8-content">
                <p>Telegram 2004, May 29, to London, not printed, requested that if mention of the
                    ownership of Ruhr properties was considered necessary in the communiqué, the
                    American Delegation was to endeavor to have the following language inserted:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The ownership question is one for future determination by the Germans
                            themselves, except insofar as past ownership will of course have been
                            affected by decartelization and denazification under due process of
                            law.” (740.00119 Council/5–2948)</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </note>
